From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anton Palgunov <toxblh@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 15:47:04 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 82/99] v8: e2k: port Maglev from loong64

Maglev for e2k is a copy of src/maglev/loong64 on top of the loong64-compatible
MacroAssembler: like loong64, e2k has no condition flags, so Maglev keeps t5
(kMaglevFlagsRegister) out of allocation and uses compare-and-branch. The
common Maglev guards for loong64 now also cover e2k; BUILD.gn lists the three
e2k files and enables Maglev on e2k by default (args.gn may still turn it off).

Two changes against the loong64 code:
- Float64Modulus calls mod_two_doubles_operation instead of the inline
  Float64Mod: the inline sequence expects a fused multiply-subtract, the e2k
  compatibility code rounds the product (2**60 % 3 gave 0 instead of 1).
- CheckJSDataViewBounds subtracts the element size from the byte length in
  64 bits and sign-extends the index (as arm64 and x64 do): the 32-bit
  subtraction made a DataView of 2 GB or more deoptimize on every access
  wider than one byte (turbolev/dataview-deopt-oob under stress_maglev).

mjsunit maglev, stress_maglev, maglev_no_turbofan: only the failures the base
already has (flush-denormals x3, math-log1p, two wasm tests).
